00:38:02.313 --> 00:38:04.525
because no one thinks
they're smart enough
for real books.

703
00:38:04.549 --> 00:38:06.694
Well. I don't have
the budget to buy
new books every semester

704
00:38:06.718 --> 00:38:08.830
when these kids
don't return them.
So. what do I do?

705
00:38:08.854 --> 00:38:10.303
Buy their books myself?

706
00:38:10.372 --> 00:38:13.172
Well. that's up to you.
but you'd be wasting
your money.

707
00:38:13.241 --> 00:38:15.441
Is there someone else
I can speak to about this?

708
00:38:16.644 --> 00:38:17.944
Excuse me?

709
00:38:18.029 --> 00:38:19.496
I'm sorry. but

710
00:38:20.231 --> 00:38:21.375
I don't understand.

711
00:38:21.399 --> 00:38:23.277
Does the Long Beach
Board of Ed agree

712
00:38:23.301 --> 00:38:25.980
that these books
should just sit here
and not be used at all?

713
00:38:26.004 --> 00:38:28.605
Let me explain.

714
00:38:28.674 --> 00:38:31.474
It's called
site-based instruction.

715
00:38:31.543 --> 00:38:34.427
It means that I
and the principal
each have the authority

716
00:38:34.496 --> 00:38:37.396
to make these kinds
of decisions without having
to go to the Board.

717
00:38:37.465 --> 00:38:39.916
who have bigger problems
to solve.

718
00:38:39.985 --> 00:38:42.519
Do you understand
how it works now?

719
00:38:42.587 --> 00:38:45.115
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to overstep
your authority.

720
00:38:45.139 --> 00:38:48.841
I would never do that.
I just...

721
00:38:48.910 --> 00:38:51.594
I don't know how to make them
interested in reading
with these.

722
00:38:51.646 --> 00:38:55.415
You can't make someone
want an education.

723
00:38:55.484 --> 00:38:59.586
The best you can do
is try to get them to obey.
to learn discipline.

724
00:38:59.654 --> 00:39:02.505
That would be a tremendous
accomplishment for them.

725
00:39:06.344 --> 00:39:08.962
Since you know Margaret
better than I do.

726
00:39:09.030 --> 00:39:11.647
if I could just get
some backup from you.

727
00:39:11.716 --> 00:39:14.150
I really think
that the stories like

728
00:39:14.219 --> 00:39:16.619
<i>The Diary of Anne Frank</i> and...

729
00:39:16.688 --> 00:39:18.499
That they'd be
so great for them.

730
00:39:18.523 --> 00:39:20.234
and she doesn't seem
to understand

731
00:39:20.258 --> 00:39:22.069
that they could relate
to these stories

732
00:39:22.093 --> 00:39:23.787
considering all that they face.

733
00:39:23.811 --> 00:39:26.763
Oh. of course.
It's a universal story.

734
00:39:26.831 --> 00:39:30.232
I mean. Anne Frank. Rodney King.

735
00:39:30.301 --> 00:39:32.334
they're almost interchangeable.

736
00:39:32.987 --> 00:39:35.454
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

737
00:39:35.523 --> 00:39:37.656
Are you making fun of me?
Yeah.

738
00:39:37.742 --> 00:39:39.926
God. listen
to what you're saying.

739
00:39:39.995 --> 00:39:41.961
How dare you compare them
to Anne Frank?

740
00:39:42.831 --> 00:39:44.146
They don't hide.

741
00:39:44.215 --> 00:39:46.616
They drive around in the open
with automatic weapons.

742
00:39:46.685 --> 00:39:48.251
I'm the one living in fear.

743
00:39:48.320 --> 00:39:50.687
I can't walk out
my door at night.

744
00:39:50.756 --> 00:39:52.672
And you blame these kids?

745
00:39:52.740 --> 00:39:56.058
This was an A-list school
before they came here.

746
00:39:56.127 --> 00:39:58.728
And look what
they turned it into.

747
00:39:58.797 --> 00:40:01.931
I mean. does it make sense

748
00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:04.200
that kids who want
an education should suffer

749
00:40:04.269 --> 00:40:07.270
because their high school
gets turned into
a reform school?

750
00:40:07.338 --> 00:40:10.039
Because kids
who don't want to be here.
and shouldn't be here.

751
00:40:10.108 --> 00:40:14.027
are forced to be here
by the geniuses
running the school district?

752
00:40:14.996 --> 00:40:16.813
Integration's a lie.

753
00:40:16.865 --> 00:40:18.564
Oh. yeah. we teachers.
we can't say that

754
00:40:18.632 --> 00:40:20.617
or we lose our jobs
for being racist.

755
00:40:20.685 --> 00:40:23.802
So. please.
stop your cheerleading. Erin.
You're ridiculous.

756
00:40:23.871 --> 00:40:26.372
You don't know
the first thing
about these kids.

757
00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:28.770
And you're not qualified
to make judgments
about the teachers

758
00:40:28.794 --> 00:40:30.927
who have to survive this place.

759
00:40:33.214 --> 00:40:35.180
(CLEARING THROAT)

760
00:40:35.249 --> 00:40:36.950
<i>(LISTEN</i>
BY TALIB KWELI PLAYING)

761
00:40:37.652 --> 00:40:39.485
<i>♪ Listen</i>

762
00:40:40.222 --> 00:40:41.805
<i>♪ Listen</i>

763
00:40:42.674 --> 00:40:45.141
<i>♪ Listen. listen</i>

764
00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:46.609
<i>♪ Listen</i>

765
00:40:47.545 --> 00:40:49.846
<i>♪ Listen</i>

766
00:40:49.915 --> 00:40:52.949
<i>♪ There's something
I want to tell you</i>

767
00:40:53.017 --> 00:40:55.885
<i>♪ Wake up. wake up.
wake up a minute</i>

768
00:40:59.858 --> 00:41:01.240
<i>♪ Listen</i>

769
00:41:02.828 --> 00:41:06.028
<i>♪ Wake up. wake up.
wake up a minute</i>

770
00:41:07.933 --> 00:41:10.917
<i>♪ Wake up. wake up.
wake up a minute ♪</i>

771
00:41:10.986 --> 00:41:12.886
We're gonna play a game.
all right?

772
00:41:12.954 --> 00:41:14.787
It's a lot of fun. I promise.

773
00:41:14.856 --> 00:41:16.438
(STUDENTS MURMURING)

774
00:41:16.507 --> 00:41:18.886
Look. you can either
sit in your seats reading
those workbooks.

775
00:41:18.910 --> 00:41:20.209
or you can play a game.

776
00:41:20.278 --> 00:41:21.706
Either way.
you're in here
till the bell rings.

777
00:41:21.730 --> 00:41:25.681
Okay. This is called
the Line Game.

778
00:41:25.750 --> 00:41:27.332
I'm gonna ask you a question.

779
00:41:27.401 --> 00:41:30.653
If that question
applies to you.
you step onto the line.

780
00:41:30.722 --> 00:41:33.289
and then step back away
for the next question.

781
00:41:33.357 --> 00:41:34.307
Easy. right?

782
00:41:34.375 --> 00:41:35.569
GIRL: Yeah. whatever.

783
00:41:35.593 --> 00:41:36.976
The first question.

784
00:41:37.044 --> 00:41:40.446
how many of you have
the new Snoop Dogg album?

785
00:41:40.515 --> 00:41:42.999
(ALL CHATTERING)

786
00:41:48.439 --> 00:41:49.605
Did you steal it?

787
00:41:50.342 --> 00:41:52.392
ERIN: Okay. back away.

788
00:41:54.929 --> 00:41:56.228
Next question.

789
00:41:56.297 --> 00:41:59.932
how many of you have seen
<i>Boyz n the Hood?</i>

790
00:42:00.001 --> 00:42:02.802
(ALL CHATTERING)

791
00:42:08.460 --> 00:42:10.460
Okay. Next question.

792
00:42:10.528 --> 00:42:13.462
How many of you
live in the projects?

793
00:42:18.203 --> 00:42:23.222
How many of you know someone.
a friend or relative.

794
00:42:23.291 --> 00:42:26.341
who was or is
in juvenile hall or jail?

795
00:42:30.215 --> 00:42:35.117
How many of you have been
in juvenile hall or jail
for any length of time?

796
00:42:35.186 --> 00:42:36.853
BOY: Detention don't count.

797
00:42:36.921 --> 00:42:37.970
(BOY CHUCKLING)

798
00:42:40.007 --> 00:42:41.991
Does a refugee camp count?

799
00:42:42.843 --> 00:42:44.661
You decide.

800
00:42:59.244 --> 00:43:02.061
How many of you know
where to get drugs right now?

801
00:43:07.318 --> 00:43:10.202
How many of you
know someone in a gang?

802
00:43:18.480 --> 00:43:21.214
How many of you
are gang members?

803
00:43:22.383 --> 00:43:24.333
GIRL 1: Nice try.
GIRL 2: Nice try.

804
00:43:25.420 --> 00:43:28.271
Okay. that was
a stupid question.
wasn't it?

805
00:43:28.339 --> 00:43:29.489
Yeah.

806
00:43:29.557 --> 00:43:31.468
You're not allowed
gang affiliations in school.

807
00:43:31.492 --> 00:43:33.943
I apologize for asking.
My badness.

808
00:43:34.012 --> 00:43:36.345
(ALL LAUGHING)

809
00:43:38.683 --> 00:43:43.285
Okay. now I'm gonna ask you
a more serious question.

810
00:43:43.354 --> 00:43:48.174
Stand on the line
if you've lost a friend
to gang violence.

811
00:44:13.701 --> 00:44:16.686
Stay on the line
if you've lost
more than one friend.

812
00:44:23.495 --> 00:44:24.727
Three.

813
00:44:38.459 --> 00:44:40.292
Four or more.

814
00:44:50.988 --> 00:44:53.156
Okay.
I'd like us to pay respect
to those people now.

815
00:44:53.224 --> 00:44:55.791
Wherever you are.
just speak their name.

816
00:44:55.843 --> 00:44:58.060
(STUDENTS WHISPERING)

817
00:45:04.836 --> 00:45:06.035
James.

818
00:45:10.591 --> 00:45:12.008
Beatriz.

819
00:45:22.637 --> 00:45:25.705
Thank you all very much.

820
00:45:25.773 --> 00:45:28.441
Now. I have something
for each of you.

821
00:45:31.229 --> 00:45:33.429
Everyone has their own story.

822
00:45:33.497 --> 00:45:38.050
and it's important for you
to tell your own story.
even to yourself.

823
00:45:38.119 --> 00:45:40.752
So. what we're going to do is

824
00:45:40.822 --> 00:45:44.073
we're gonna write every day
in these journals.

825
00:45:44.142 --> 00:45:46.269
You can write about
whatever you want.

826
00:45:46.293 --> 00:45:48.744
the past.
the present. the future.

827
00:45:48.813 --> 00:45:52.748
You can write
it like a diary.
or you can write

828
00:45:52.817 --> 00:45:58.104
songs. poems. any good thing.
bad thing. anything.

829
00:45:58.172 --> 00:46:01.107
But you have to write every day.

830
00:46:01.175 --> 00:46:04.727
Keep a pen nearby.
Whenever you feel
the inspiration.

831
00:46:04.796 --> 00:46:06.896
And they won't be graded.

832
00:46:06.964 --> 00:46:10.666
How can I give an A or a B
for writing the truth. right?

833
00:46:10.734 --> 00:46:13.519
And I will not read them
unless you give me
permission.

834
00:46:13.588 --> 00:46:17.356
I will need to see
that you've made an entry.
but I'll... I'll just do this.

835
00:46:17.425 --> 00:46:19.065
skim to see
that you wrote that day.

836
00:46:19.093 --> 00:46:21.827
Now. if you want me
to read it. I have...

837
00:46:21.896 --> 00:46:24.397
Excuse me.
A cabinet over here.

838
00:46:24.465 --> 00:46:28.166
It has a lock on it.
I will keep it
open during class.

839
00:46:28.235 --> 00:46:31.103
and you can leave
your diary there
if you want me to read it.

840
00:46:31.171 --> 00:46:34.840
I will lock this cabinet
at the end of every class.

841
00:46:36.060 --> 00:46:37.260
Okay?

842
00:46:39.163 --> 00:46:42.198
So. you can each come up.
one by one.

843
00:46:42.266 --> 00:46:45.034
and take your own journal.

844
00:46:52.443 --> 00:46:54.343
Whenever you're ready.

845
00:47:18.987 --> 00:47:21.548
ERIN: Eva holds back.
but I know she
wants to be involved.

846
00:47:21.572 --> 00:47:23.105
She's so stubborn.

847
00:47:23.174 --> 00:47:25.569
Who really surprised me
was Brandy.
who never says a word.

848
00:47:25.593 --> 00:47:28.405
but she was the first
to step up and take
a journal. I...

849
00:47:28.429 --> 00:47:30.295
Honey. here. Here. sit down.

850
00:47:30.364 --> 00:47:31.975
It's all right.
No. it's all right.
I'll move this.

851
00:47:31.999 --> 00:47:34.283
I don't mind standing.
Food goes straight down.

852
00:47:34.352 --> 00:47:36.052
How much longer
are you gonna be?

853
00:47:36.120 --> 00:47:37.369
I don't know.

854
00:47:37.438 --> 00:47:39.916
Want to help?
Not really.
I'm a terrible drawer.

855
00:47:39.940 --> 00:47:41.524
You're an architect.

856
00:47:41.592 --> 00:47:45.193
Hmm. All right.
I... I just don't want to.

857
00:47:45.262 --> 00:47:46.857
What's the matter?
Is something wrong?

858
00:47:46.881 --> 00:47:49.531
No. it's nothing.

859
00:47:49.600 --> 00:47:53.535
Well. it's just. you know.
I want to hear all this.
I do.

860
00:47:53.604 --> 00:47:54.737
It just...

861
00:47:54.806 --> 00:47:57.106
I feel like we haven't
talked about anything.

862
00:47:57.175 --> 00:47:59.775
other than your job.
in like forever.

863
00:47:59.844 --> 00:48:02.945
I'm sorry. Well.
what's going on at work?

864
00:48:03.014 --> 00:48:05.381
Nothing.
I don't want to talk
about that. either.

865
00:48:05.450 --> 00:48:08.283
I just want to hang out.
I want to be home.

866
00:48:10.671 --> 00:48:13.222
And I want to be
with my schoolteacher.

867
00:48:19.781 --> 00:48:22.998
I've always had this fantasy
about being kept
late after school.

868
00:48:23.067 --> 00:48:27.753
Well. I'm sorry I left
my dirty erasers at work.

869
00:48:27.822 --> 00:48:30.239
Do all the other teachers
put in this much
extra effort?

870
00:48:30.308 --> 00:48:33.125
I don't know.
I'm kind of making it up
as I go along.

871
00:48:33.193 --> 00:48:34.938
And the other teachers
don't really talk to me.

872
00:48:34.962 --> 00:48:37.124
I mean. Brian and Margaret...
Honey.
I don't want to think.

873
00:48:37.148 --> 00:48:38.741
I'm sorry.
Okay. don't think.
I just wanna...

874
00:48:38.765 --> 00:48:40.516
I'm almost done. okay?

875
00:48:42.120 --> 00:48:44.220
So. how much longer?

876
00:48:45.189 --> 00:48:47.506
Not long. Promise.

877
00:48:51.445 --> 00:48:54.763
BRIAN: Thank you so much
for coming. Susan's a terrific
student. Thank you.

878
00:48:54.832 --> 00:48:56.493
Great to see you.
Good night. Take care.

879
00:48:56.517 --> 00:48:58.500
Jim. thank you so much.
Thanks. Brian.

880
00:48:58.569 --> 00:49:00.786
I appreciate you guys coming
to Parents' Night.

881
00:49:00.855 --> 00:49:02.254
Drive safe.

882
00:49:17.155 --> 00:49:18.570
(DOOR CLOSING)

883
00:49:22.259 --> 00:49:23.993
(KEYS JINGLING)

884
00:49:43.130 --> 00:49:46.198
<i>BRANDY: In every war.
there is an enemy.</i>

885
00:49:46.267 --> 00:49:48.567
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

886
00:49:52.790 --> 00:49:56.058
<i>I watched my mother
being half beaten to death</i>

887
00:49:56.127 --> 00:50:00.278
<i>and watched</i>
<i>as blood and tears</i>
<i>streamed down her face.</i>

888
00:50:00.347 --> 00:50:05.167
<i>I felt useless and scared
and furious at the same time.</i>

889
00:50:05.236 --> 00:50:07.036
Stay there. Brandy.
Watch the kids!

890
00:50:07.105 --> 00:50:09.855
Get my money!
Watch the kids!

891
00:50:09.924 --> 00:50:14.210
<i>I can still feel</i>
<i>the sting of the belt</i>
<i>on my back and my legs.</i>

892
00:50:14.278 --> 00:50:17.045
<i>One time.
he couldn't pay the rent.</i>

893
00:50:17.114 --> 00:50:18.892
<i>And that night
he stopped us on the street</i>

894
00:50:18.916 --> 00:50:20.582
<i>and pointed to the concrete.</i>

895
00:50:20.651 --> 00:50:22.801
<i>He said. "Pick a spot."</i>

896
00:50:34.548 --> 00:50:36.381
<i>MARCUS: Clive was my boy.</i>

897
00:50:36.450 --> 00:50:38.450
<i>He had my back plenty of times.</i>

898
00:50:38.486 --> 00:50:42.504
<i>We was like one fist.
me and him. one army.</i>

899
00:50:42.573 --> 00:50:44.790
That's heavy.
Yeah.

900
00:50:46.360 --> 00:50:48.560
That's the real shit right here.

901
00:50:48.629 --> 00:50:50.763
Nobody'll jump us now.

902
00:50:50.831 --> 00:50:53.732
But we got to practice
'cause this. this got power.

903
00:50:53.801 --> 00:50:55.134
You shoot it. it...

904
00:50:55.202 --> 00:50:56.935
(GUN FIRES)

905
00:51:01.676 --> 00:51:05.210
<i>I sat there
till the police came.</i>

906
00:51:05.279 --> 00:51:08.058
<i>(CHATTERING ON POLICE RADIO)</i>
<i>But when they come.</i>
<i>all they see is a dead body.</i>

907
00:51:08.082 --> 00:51:10.565
<i>a gun and a nigga.</i>

908
00:51:10.634 --> 00:51:12.601
<i>They took me to juvenile hall.</i>

909
00:51:12.669 --> 00:51:14.603
<i>First night was the scariest.</i>

910
00:51:14.672 --> 00:51:17.189
(BOYS SCREAMING)

911
00:51:17.257 --> 00:51:19.308
<i>Inmates banging on the walls.</i>

912
00:51:19.360 --> 00:51:20.971
<i>throwing up their gang signs.</i>

913
00:51:20.995 --> 00:51:23.645
<i>yelling out who they were.
where they're from.</i>

914
00:51:23.714 --> 00:51:25.914
<i>I cried my first night.</i>

915
00:51:25.983 --> 00:51:28.583
<i>Can't never let
nobody know that.</i>

916
00:51:28.652 --> 00:51:31.220
<i>I spent the next few years
in and out of cells.</i>

917
00:51:31.288 --> 00:51:34.123
<i>Every day I'd worry.
"When will I be free?"</i>

918
00:51:37.694 --> 00:51:40.595
My brother taught me
what the life is
for a young black man.

919
00:51:40.664 --> 00:51:44.116
Do what you have to.
pimp. deal. whatever.

920
00:51:44.184 --> 00:51:46.635
Learn what colors to learn.
gang boundaries.

921
00:51:46.703 --> 00:51:49.016
You can stay on one corner.
you can't stay on another.

922
00:51:49.040 --> 00:51:50.406
<i>ANDRE: Learn to be quiet.</i>

923
00:51:50.474 --> 00:51:51.802
<i>A wrong word can get you popped.</i>

924
00:51:51.826 --> 00:51:54.960
If you look in my eyes.
you'll see a loving girl.

925
00:51:55.029 --> 00:51:58.463
If you look at my smile.
you'll see nothing wrong.

926
00:51:58.532 --> 00:52:01.867
<i>GLORIA:</i>
<i>If you pull up my shirt.</i>
<i>you'll see the bruises.</i>

927
00:52:01.935 --> 00:52:04.102
<i>What did I do
to make him so mad?</i>

928
00:52:04.171 --> 00:52:08.674
<i>JAMAL: At 16.</i>
<i>I've seen more dead bodies</i>
<i>than a mortician.</i>

929
00:52:08.743 --> 00:52:10.186
<i>Every time I step out my door.</i>

930
00:52:10.210 --> 00:52:13.044
<i>I'm faced with the risk
of being shot.</i>

931
00:52:13.113 --> 00:52:14.613
<i>To the outside world.</i>

932
00:52:14.682 --> 00:52:17.716
<i>it's just another dead body
on the street corner.</i>

933
00:52:17.785 --> 00:52:19.825
<i>They don't know
that he was my friend.</i>

934
00:52:19.854 --> 00:52:21.331
<i>SINDY:
During the war in Cambodia.</i>

935
00:52:21.355 --> 00:52:23.355
<i>the camp stripped away
my father's dignity.</i>

936
00:52:23.424 --> 00:52:25.957
<i>He sometimes tries
to hurt my mom and me.</i>

937
00:52:26.026 --> 00:52:28.226
I feel like I have to
protect my family.

938
00:52:28.295 --> 00:52:31.463
I was having trouble
deciding what candy
I wanted.

939
00:52:31.532 --> 00:52:33.331
then I heard gunshots.

940
00:52:33.401 --> 00:52:35.267
I looked down to see
that one of my friends

941
00:52:35.335 --> 00:52:39.054
had blood coming out
of his back and his mouth.

942
00:52:39.123 --> 00:52:42.308
The next day.
I pulled up my shirt
and got strapped with a gun

943
00:52:42.376 --> 00:52:44.876
I found in an alley by my house.

944
00:52:44.946 --> 00:52:47.124
<i>EVA: I don't even know
how this war started.</i>

945
00:52:47.148 --> 00:52:50.215
<i>It's just two sides</i>
<i>who tripped each other</i>
<i>way back.</i>

946
00:52:50.283 --> 00:52:53.485
<i>Who cares about
the history behind it?</i>

947
00:52:53.553 --> 00:52:55.020
<i>I am my father's daughter.</i>

948
00:52:55.089 --> 00:52:57.055
<i>And when they call me
to testify.</i>

949
00:52:57.124 --> 00:52:59.491
<i>I will protect
my own no matter what.</i>

950
00:52:59.559 --> 00:53:01.293
<i>TITO: Nobody cares what I do.</i>

951
00:53:01.361 --> 00:53:03.796
<i>Why should I bother
coming to school?</i>

952
00:53:03.864 --> 00:53:07.532
<i>MARCUS: My friends</i>
<i>are soldiers. not of war.</i>
<i>but of the streets.</i>

953
00:53:07.601 --> 00:53:09.467
<i>They fight for their lives.</i>

954
00:53:09.536 --> 00:53:12.048
<i>ALEJANDRO: I hate</i>
<i>the cold feeling of a gun</i>
<i>against my skin.</i>

955
00:53:12.072 --> 00:53:13.404
<i>It makes me shiver.</i>

956
00:53:13.473 --> 00:53:15.074
<i>It's a crazy-ass life.</i>

957
00:53:15.142 --> 00:53:17.242
<i>Once you're in.
there's no getting out.</i>

958
00:53:17.311 --> 00:53:19.011
<i>MARCUS:
Every time I jump somebody in</i>

959
00:53:19.080 --> 00:53:22.247
<i>and make someone</i>
<i>a part of our gang.</i>
<i>it's another baptism.</i>

960
00:53:22.316 --> 00:53:24.800
<i>They give us their life.
we give them a new one.</i>

961
00:53:24.868 --> 00:53:28.186
I've lost many friends
who have died
in an undeclared war.

962
00:53:29.423 --> 00:53:32.357
To the soldiers and me.
it's all worth it.

963
00:53:32.426 --> 00:53:36.128
Risk your life
dodging bullets.
pulling triggers.

964
00:53:37.498 --> 00:53:39.164
It's all worth it.

965
00:53:56.817 --> 00:53:59.117
Rum and Coke.
Oh. man.

966
00:54:00.020 --> 00:54:01.219
This is...

967
00:54:01.288 --> 00:54:03.405
Mr. Gruwell?
Your table is ready.

968
00:54:03.474 --> 00:54:05.424
Follow me.

969
00:54:05.493 --> 00:54:08.593
Dad. I got them.
Okay.

970
00:54:08.662 --> 00:54:11.130
Dad. I don't know
what to do with this.

971
00:54:11.198 --> 00:54:13.665
I'm not a social worker.
I'm barely a teacher.

972
00:54:13.734 --> 00:54:14.900
Thank you.

973
00:54:14.968 --> 00:54:18.037
These kids.
they're 14. 15 years old.

974
00:54:18.105 --> 00:54:20.855
and if they make it
through the day alive.
that's good enough.

975
00:54:20.924 --> 00:54:22.908
And I'm supposed to teach them?

976
00:54:25.796 --> 00:54:27.345
Listen to me.

977
00:54:27.414 --> 00:54:32.551
You're not responsible
for their lives
outside that classroom.

978
00:54:32.620 --> 00:54:35.620
Just do your job
the best you can.
How?

979
00:54:35.689 --> 00:54:38.034
The administration
doesn't give me
any resources.

980
00:54:38.058 --> 00:54:39.924
no books. no support.

981
00:54:41.712 --> 00:54:43.378
So. what should I do?

982
00:54:46.683 --> 00:54:49.362
Fulfill your obligation
till the end
of the school year.

983
00:54:49.386 --> 00:54:52.087
but line up another position.

984
00:54:52.156 --> 00:54:55.574
Success follows experience.

985
00:54:55.642 --> 00:54:57.976
So. get some more experience.

986
00:54:59.780 --> 00:55:04.733
But no matter what.
you gotta remember.
it's just a job.

987
00:55:04.802 --> 00:55:08.042
If you're not right
for this one.
get another job.

988
00:55:11.041 --> 00:55:14.425
You're gonna sell bras
at a department store?
Just part-time.

989
00:55:14.494 --> 00:55:17.107
I'm having a little trouble
getting books and things
for the kids.

990
00:55:17.131 --> 00:55:19.509
So. a little extra money
will give me
a little more freedom

991
00:55:19.533 --> 00:55:20.982
to do what I want.

992
00:55:21.051 --> 00:55:23.180
And this way
you can play tennis
with Evan after work.

993
00:55:23.204 --> 00:55:25.287
Okay. let me
get my head around this.

994
00:55:25.356 --> 00:55:28.907
You're going to get
an extra job
to pay for your job.

995
00:55:28.976 --> 00:55:31.059
It's just temporary.
I promise.

996
00:55:31.128 --> 00:55:34.229
Once the kids' grades go up.
I'll get a little more help
from the school.

997
00:55:34.297 --> 00:55:37.365
And I get
an employee's discount.
Isn't that great?

998
00:55:37.434 --> 00:55:40.585
Want a new TV?
Yeah.

999
00:55:54.468 --> 00:55:57.002
Um. excuse me.
if I wanted to order
any books in bulk.

1000
00:55:57.071 --> 00:55:58.570
could I get
some sort of a discount?

1001
00:56:03.510 --> 00:56:05.791
These books are brand new.
I know.

1002
00:56:06.847 --> 00:56:09.965
Okay. guys. gals.
Listen up.

1003
00:56:10.034 --> 00:56:12.045
The only problem
with this book is

1004
00:56:12.069 --> 00:56:14.030
it's about a gang member
and there's violence in it.

1005
00:56:14.054 --> 00:56:16.449
so you may not be able
to read it as part
of the curriculum.

1006
00:56:16.473 --> 00:56:20.308
So. I'm going to try my best
to get permission. all right?

1007
00:56:22.580 --> 00:56:24.796
It's been a little difficult
getting their attention.

1008
00:56:24.865 --> 00:56:26.593
Up until recently.
the only thing they hated

1009
00:56:26.617 --> 00:56:28.817
more than each other was me.

1010
00:56:28.886 --> 00:56:32.437
Well. you united them
and that's a step.

1011
00:56:33.773 --> 00:56:35.974
What can I do for you?

1012
00:56:36.042 --> 00:56:37.776
I want to do more with them.

1013
00:56:37.845 --> 00:56:40.912
and I need the support
of someone in power.

1014
00:56:40.981 --> 00:56:43.960
You have to take this up
with your department head
and your principal.

1015
00:56:43.984 --> 00:56:46.028
I can't get involved
in inner school policy.

1016
00:56:46.052 --> 00:56:48.470
My principal only listens
to my department head.

1017
00:56:48.539 --> 00:56:50.388
and she's not very supportive.

1018
00:56:50.457 --> 00:56:52.268
You'll have to find a way
to deal with it.

1019
00:56:52.292 --> 00:56:55.143
No. I'd rather
just deal directly
with someone in power.

1020
00:56:55.211 --> 00:56:57.378
Ms. Gruwell.
there's a system in place

1021
00:56:57.447 --> 00:57:00.381
based on years of running
an educational facility.

1022
00:57:00.450 --> 00:57:01.962
You have to follow that system.

1023
00:57:01.986 --> 00:57:03.368
No. I won't.

1024
00:57:03.436 --> 00:57:04.586
(PHONES RINGING)

1025
00:57:04.654 --> 00:57:07.605
Look. I'm just trying
to do my job here.

1026
00:57:07.674 --> 00:57:10.408
What's the point
of a voluntary
integration program

1027
00:57:10.477 --> 00:57:12.077
if the kids making
it to high school

1028
00:57:12.146 --> 00:57:13.512
have a 5th grade reading level?

1029
00:57:13.580 --> 00:57:15.431
I enforced that program.

1030
00:57:15.499 --> 00:57:16.765
With all due respect.

1031
00:57:16.834 --> 00:57:19.100
all that program is doing
is warehousing these kids

1032
00:57:19.169 --> 00:57:20.647
until they're old enough
to disappear.

1033
00:57:20.671 --> 00:57:22.398
Look. I appreciate
your intentions.

1034
00:57:22.422 --> 00:57:25.057
but there's nothing I can do
on a class-by-class basis.

1035
00:57:25.125 --> 00:57:28.693
Dr. Cohn.
why should they waste
their time showing up

1036
00:57:28.762 --> 00:57:31.496
when they know
we're wasting our time
teaching them?

1037
00:57:31.565 --> 00:57:34.333
We tell them. "Go to school.
Get an education."

1038
00:57:34.401 --> 00:57:36.467
And then we say.
"Well. they can't learn.

1039
00:57:36.536 --> 00:57:38.804
"so let's not
waste resources."

1040
00:57:38.872 --> 00:57:40.422
I'm thinking trips.

1041
00:57:40.491 --> 00:57:43.374
Most of them have never
been outside of Long Beach.

1042
00:57:43.443 --> 00:57:45.994
They haven't been given
the opportunity

1043
00:57:46.062 --> 00:57:48.597
to expand their thinking
about what's out there
for them.

1044
00:57:48.665 --> 00:57:50.126
And they're hungry for it.
I know it.

1045
00:57:50.150 --> 00:57:52.167
And it's purely a reward system.

1046
00:57:52.235 --> 00:57:54.252
They won't get anything
they haven't earned

1047
00:57:54.321 --> 00:57:56.354
by doing their work
and upping their grades.

1048
00:57:56.423 --> 00:57:57.934
But if Ms. Campbell
won't give you books

1049
00:57:57.958 --> 00:57:59.135
because of budget restrictions.

1050
00:57:59.159 --> 00:58:00.620
she's not gonna approve
school trips.

1051
00:58:00.644 --> 00:58:01.909
I'll raise the money.

1052
00:58:01.978 --> 00:58:04.997
I just need to know
I won't meet resistance.

1053
00:58:05.065 --> 00:58:07.215
See. I can't promise
them anything
I can't deliver.

1054
00:58:07.284 --> 00:58:09.751
It only proves
what they already believe.

1055
00:58:11.655 --> 00:58:15.873
All I'm saying is.
Ms. Campbell doesn't need
to be bothered.

1056
00:58:15.942 --> 00:58:16.958
(CHUCKLES)

1057
00:58:18.995 --> 00:58:20.840
You're a concierge
at the Marriott?

1058
00:58:20.864 --> 00:58:24.082
It's just weekends.
You play tennis
with Evan on Saturdays.

1059
00:58:24.151 --> 00:58:26.084
And you can play golf
with my dad on Sundays.

1060
00:58:26.152 --> 00:58:27.480
Oh. you want me to play golf?

1061
00:58:27.504 --> 00:58:29.621
And the bonus is
I get employee rates

1062
00:58:29.689 --> 00:58:31.990
on Marriott hotel rooms
all over the world.

1063
00:58:32.059 --> 00:58:33.303
I've heard a lot of hyphenates.

1064
00:58:33.327 --> 00:58:35.338
but a bra-selling-
English-teacher-
hotel-concierge

1065
00:58:35.362 --> 00:58:36.911
has gotta be a new one.

1066
00:58:36.980 --> 00:58:39.342
You told me
your part-time job
was temporary.

1067
00:58:39.366 --> 00:58:42.367
It is.
I just don't know
for how long.

1068
00:58:42.435 --> 00:58:44.419
What if I said no?
No. what?

1069
00:58:44.488 --> 00:58:46.955
No. I don't want you
working three jobs.

1070
00:58:47.023 --> 00:58:49.269
But I can make
it work. Scott.
No. that's not the point.

1071
00:58:49.293 --> 00:58:51.638
You can do anything!
We know that already.

1072
00:58:51.662 --> 00:58:55.279
It's just that I... You...

1073
00:58:55.348 --> 00:58:56.915
You didn't even ask me.

1074
00:58:56.984 --> 00:58:59.451
I'm just trying
to do my job. Scott.

1075
00:58:59.519 --> 00:59:01.603
By getting two more jobs?

1076
00:59:02.422 --> 00:59:05.206
I don't understand. Erin.

1077
00:59:05.275 --> 00:59:07.876
Scott. this is our time
to go after what we want.

1078
00:59:07.945 --> 00:59:11.330
when we're young.
before we have a family.

1079
00:59:11.398 --> 00:59:13.894
Maybe this is
the perfect time for you
to go back to school.

1080
00:59:13.918 --> 00:59:15.934
get your architect's degree.

1081
00:59:16.003 --> 00:59:17.952
Wouldn't that be great?

1082
00:59:20.975 --> 00:59:22.473
What?

1083
00:59:24.127 --> 00:59:25.743
Nothing.

1084
00:59:25.812 --> 00:59:27.261
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

1085
00:59:32.152 --> 00:59:34.130
So. I'll call you
with a list of venues.

1086
00:59:34.154 --> 00:59:36.248
I've scheduled
a PTA board meeting
for next week.

1087
00:59:36.272 --> 00:59:37.517
So. it should be no problem.

1088
00:59:37.541 --> 00:59:38.851
Thank you so much.
You're welcome.

1089
00:59:38.875 --> 00:59:40.470
Lovely to see you. Paula.
Good to see you. too.

1090
00:59:40.494 --> 00:59:42.610
Hi.
Hello.

1091
00:59:42.679 --> 00:59:43.973
Principal Banning
received a call

1092
00:59:43.997 --> 00:59:45.831
