1109
01:00:33.063 --> 01:00:34.413
Andre Bryant.

1110
01:00:34.481 --> 01:00:35.681
Andre.

1111
01:00:39.353 --> 01:00:41.764
<i>ANDRE: Since my pop split.
my mom can't even look at me.</i>

1112
01:00:41.788 --> 01:00:43.955
<i>'cause I look like my dad.</i>

1113
01:00:44.024 --> 01:00:45.857
<i>And with my brother in jail.</i>

1114
01:00:45.926 --> 01:00:49.160
<i>she looks at me and thinks
that's where I'm going. too.</i>

1115
01:00:49.229 --> 01:00:51.396
<i>She doesn't see me.</i>

1116
01:00:51.464 --> 01:00:53.531
<i>She doesn't see me at all.</i>

1117
01:00:58.105 --> 01:00:59.637
I'm going out.

1118
01:01:01.908 --> 01:01:03.558
(PEOPLE SHOUTING)

1119
01:01:05.128 --> 01:01:06.272
What up?
Hey.

1120
01:01:06.296 --> 01:01:08.546
Where you going?
I need you.

1121
01:01:08.615 --> 01:01:10.098
No. man. I can't now.

1122
01:01:10.167 --> 01:01:11.599
I got something to do.

1123
01:01:11.668 --> 01:01:13.334
Tonight. I'll do it tonight.

1124
01:01:13.403 --> 01:01:15.381
I gotta go do something.
and I can't carry that
around with me.

1125
01:01:15.405 --> 01:01:16.838
(SCOFFS)

1126
01:01:16.907 --> 01:01:18.802
Forget it. man.
I'll get somebody else.

1127
01:01:18.826 --> 01:01:21.107
I can't be waiting
all day on you.

1128
01:01:21.544 --> 01:01:22.664
Hey.

1129
01:01:24.113 --> 01:01:25.891
Sorry about your brother. man.

1130
01:01:25.915 --> 01:01:27.794
I hear he going away for life.

1131
01:01:27.818 --> 01:01:30.284
They won't get it.
The guy he was with
confessed.

1132
01:01:30.353 --> 01:01:32.504
To who? Your brother?

1133
01:01:33.173 --> 01:01:35.606
Hey. You Andre?

1134
01:01:47.037 --> 01:01:48.570
What up?
Hey.

1135
01:01:54.327 --> 01:01:55.360
What?

1136
01:01:55.428 --> 01:01:57.145
Put on your seat belt.

1137
01:02:00.134 --> 01:02:01.966
You. too. young lady.

1138
01:02:05.472 --> 01:02:08.173
You kids ever been
to Newport Beach before?

1139
01:02:08.241 --> 01:02:11.909
What?
We went there last year
on our way to Paris.

1140
01:02:18.118 --> 01:02:19.618
Paris.

1141
01:02:21.071 --> 01:02:22.687
(GATE BUZZING)

1142
01:02:23.991 --> 01:02:27.008
It's good.
I brought you something.

1143
01:02:31.081 --> 01:02:33.732
It's a good book.
I read it in school.

1144
01:02:33.800 --> 01:02:37.636
It's about a gang kid.
and I thought you
might like to read it.

1145
01:02:40.640 --> 01:02:43.074
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1146
01:02:45.829 --> 01:02:48.162
He told me what I had to say
when I'm on the stand.

1147
01:02:49.700 --> 01:02:52.050
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1148
01:03:27.937 --> 01:03:29.204
(CELL DOOR CLOSING)

1149
01:03:44.488 --> 01:03:46.032
<i>ANDRE: At the beginning
of the tour.</i>

1150
01:03:46.056 --> 01:03:48.656
<i>they give you a card
with a child's picture on it.</i>

1151
01:03:48.725 --> 01:03:50.186
<i>You could find out who they were</i>

1152
01:03:50.210 --> 01:03:52.054
<i>and what camp they were sent to.</i>

1153
01:03:52.078 --> 01:03:56.581
<i>And at the end of the tour.</i>
<i>you could find out</i>
<i>if they survived.</i>

1154
01:03:56.650 --> 01:03:58.950
<i>I got a little girl from Italy.</i>

1155
01:04:13.283 --> 01:04:15.449
Tito. your hat.

1156
01:04:45.331 --> 01:04:47.059
<i>MAN ON RECORDING:</i>
<i>Kristallnacht.</i>
<i>they called it.</i>

1157
01:04:47.083 --> 01:04:49.000
<i>The Night of Broken Glass.</i>

1158
01:04:49.069 --> 01:04:51.435
<i>Hundreds of synagogues
looted and burned.</i>

1159
01:04:51.504 --> 01:04:54.306
<i>More than 7.000
Jewish stores destroyed.</i>

1160
01:04:54.374 --> 01:04:56.508
<i>Over 100 Jews killed.</i>

1161
01:05:09.556 --> 01:05:12.424
<i>WOMAN: A small center
for children in Isieux</i>

1162
01:05:12.492 --> 01:05:15.327
<i>in the French province of Ain.</i>

1163
01:05:15.395 --> 01:05:18.346
<i>Among the children</i>
<i>deported that day</i>
<i>to Birkenau</i>

1164
01:05:18.415 --> 01:05:21.816
<i>was 11-year-old
Liliane Berenstein.</i>

1165
01:05:21.885 --> 01:05:25.820
<i>who. before leaving.
left behind a letter to God.</i>

1166
01:05:31.628 --> 01:05:33.628
<i>ALEJANDRO:
My little boy died.</i>

1167
01:05:33.696 --> 01:05:36.697
<i>He got off the train
and they killed him.</i>

1168
01:05:36.767 --> 01:05:38.967
<i>I don't know why
it bothered me so much.</i>

1169
01:05:39.035 --> 01:05:41.435
<i>I've seen death all my life.</i>

1170
01:05:41.504 --> 01:05:46.007
<i>But this little boy
was only five.</i>

1171
01:06:07.063 --> 01:06:11.232
<i>JAMAL: Ms. G had a beautiful</i>
<i>dinner for us at the hotel</i>
<i>where she works.</i>

1172
01:06:11.301 --> 01:06:15.303
<i>She invited</i>
<i>real Holocaust survivors</i>
<i>from the museum to meet us.</i>

1173
01:06:16.406 --> 01:06:18.239
<i>There was Elisabeth Mann.</i>

1174
01:06:18.308 --> 01:06:23.077
I had my parents.
my sister. my two brothers.

1175
01:06:23.146 --> 01:06:24.662
<i>Gloria Ungar.</i>

1176
01:06:24.731 --> 01:06:27.332
If any of you
have seen someone
with a number on their arm.

1177
01:06:27.400 --> 01:06:29.534
these were the lucky people.

1178
01:06:29.603 --> 01:06:32.103
The people who.
when we came to Auschwitz.

1179
01:06:32.171 --> 01:06:36.006
when they tattooed
the people they took us
to do the slave work.

1180
01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:39.076
Not the others.
and that included
many of my family.

1181
01:06:39.145 --> 01:06:41.980
So. we ran away.
s-some of the young kids.

1182
01:06:42.048 --> 01:06:44.532
I was at that time
11-and-a-half years old.

1183
01:06:44.601 --> 01:06:45.667
<i>Eddie Ilam.</i>

1184
01:06:45.735 --> 01:06:47.780
And where to go. I didn't know.

1185
01:06:47.804 --> 01:06:51.572
but I remember one place
where I used to live.

1186
01:06:51.641 --> 01:06:54.042
So when I ran there.
there was not one Jew left.

1187
01:06:54.110 --> 01:06:57.328
I was in the worst camp.
I was in Auschwitz.

1188
01:06:57.397 --> 01:06:58.996
<i>And Renee Firestone.</i>

1189
01:06:59.065 --> 01:07:03.234
When I arrived.
my parents were immediately
taken away from me.

1190
01:07:03.303 --> 01:07:06.638
My little sister.
who was then 14 years old.

1191
01:07:06.706 --> 01:07:09.841
stayed with me
for a little while.

1192
01:07:09.910 --> 01:07:13.188
And then later on.
I was separated
from her also.

1193
01:07:13.212 --> 01:07:16.614
<i>She lost her whole family
at the camps.</i>

1194
01:07:16.683 --> 01:07:21.753
<i>She came to this country</i>
<i>with $4 in her pocket</i>
<i>and a newborn baby.</i>

1195
01:07:21.822 --> 01:07:24.055
<i>I'll never forget these people.</i>

1196
01:07:24.123 --> 01:07:26.974
MS. FIRESTONE:
And then she was killed
because they didn't want...

1197
01:07:27.044 --> 01:07:29.977
<i>I can't believe Ms. G
did all of this for us.</i>

