01:29:20.339 --> 01:29:23.690
You know
what you're gonna say
in that courtroom?

1604
01:29:23.759 --> 01:29:25.792
I know what I have to say.

1605
01:29:27.413 --> 01:29:29.112
Yeah.

1606
01:29:29.181 --> 01:29:30.714
You know how that is.

1607
01:29:30.783 --> 01:29:32.749
I know.

1608
01:29:32.818 --> 01:29:35.530
And that man
that put your father
in prison.

1609
01:29:35.554 --> 01:29:38.538
he knew he was sending
an innocent man.

1610
01:29:38.607 --> 01:29:39.939
But. you know.

1611
01:29:41.844 --> 01:29:43.477
he was just

1612
01:29:45.514 --> 01:29:47.397
protecting his own.

1613
01:29:53.404 --> 01:29:56.139
What the hell does everybody
want from me?

1614
01:29:58.577 --> 01:29:59.726
(DOG BARKING)

1615
01:30:12.441 --> 01:30:13.623
(SIREN WAILING)

1616
01:30:22.868 --> 01:30:25.251
Hey. Mama. Mama.

1617
01:30:30.459 --> 01:30:32.893
What the hell
are you doing here?

1618
01:30:39.167 --> 01:30:41.301
I want to come home.

1619
01:30:41.369 --> 01:30:43.331
I don't want to be
in the streets no more.

1620
01:30:43.355 --> 01:30:44.704
I'm sorry.

1621
01:30:47.009 --> 01:30:50.177
I want to change.
I can't do it alone.

1622
01:30:52.047 --> 01:30:53.713
I need you. Mama.

1623
01:30:55.450 --> 01:30:56.950
I need you.

1624
01:31:34.606 --> 01:31:36.406
And what time was that?

1625
01:31:37.242 --> 01:31:40.143
I told you. 9:00. 9:30.

1626
01:31:40.211 --> 01:31:41.856
And you had a clear view
of the defendant.

1627
01:31:41.880 --> 01:31:44.781
Grant Rice. in the store?

1628
01:31:44.849 --> 01:31:47.767
I told you he was playing
the video game.

1629
01:31:47.836 --> 01:31:50.671
Then what happened?
What did you see?

1630
01:31:50.739 --> 01:31:52.951
Well. he got all whacked
because he lost the game.

1631
01:31:52.975 --> 01:31:56.592
and then he started
shouting and all.
threatening everybody.

1632
01:31:56.661 --> 01:31:58.778
He threatened everyone?

1633
01:31:58.847 --> 01:32:00.914
He threatened you?

1634
01:32:00.983 --> 01:32:03.433
No. The guy
who ran the store.

1635
01:32:03.502 --> 01:32:05.502
He wanted his money back
for the game.

1636
01:32:05.571 --> 01:32:07.670
And what did the store owner do?

1637
01:32:08.524 --> 01:32:10.189
He shouted back.

1638
01:32:10.258 --> 01:32:12.025
And they were fighting.

1639
01:32:12.093 --> 01:32:14.227
Then he. the defendant.

1640
01:32:14.295 --> 01:32:16.913
knocked something over
and left the store.

1641
01:32:16.982 --> 01:32:19.449
And then what happened?
What did you see?

1642
01:32:23.589 --> 01:32:25.255
I saw...

1643
01:32:37.385 --> 01:32:38.885
I saw...

1644
01:32:54.136 --> 01:32:56.152
Paco did it.

1645
01:32:56.221 --> 01:32:57.837
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

1646
01:32:59.775 --> 01:33:01.591
Paco killed the guy.

1647
01:33:27.669 --> 01:33:30.270
(MAN SHOUTING IN SPANISH)

1648
01:33:33.175 --> 01:33:34.407
(DOG BARKING)

1649
01:33:38.814 --> 01:33:39.896
(SHOUTS
IN SPANISH)

1650
01:33:53.528 --> 01:33:55.328
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1651
01:34:27.162 --> 01:34:29.696
My father won't
talk to me anymore.

1652
01:34:32.033 --> 01:34:34.734
And I have to lay low
for a little while

1653
01:34:34.803 --> 01:34:37.437
because there's word out
to jump me.

1654
01:34:38.807 --> 01:34:41.124
So I'm gonna be
living with my aunt.

1655
01:34:42.577 --> 01:34:47.313
See. uh. my aunt lives
even further away.

1656
01:34:49.584 --> 01:34:53.920
so I was just wondering
if I could. like. uh.

1657
01:34:57.025 --> 01:35:00.676
stay here late with you

1658
01:35:02.447 --> 01:35:04.280
so I can get my homework done.

1659
01:35:04.349 --> 01:35:07.383
'cause it's late
by the time I get home.

1660
01:35:09.487 --> 01:35:13.757
You can stay
as late as you want.

1661
01:35:13.825 --> 01:35:17.676
And I can even drive you
to your aunt's.
if it gets too late.

1662
01:35:17.745 --> 01:35:19.094
(LAUGHS)

1663
01:35:21.032 --> 01:35:22.898
Ms. G. let's not get nuts.

1664
01:35:58.570 --> 01:36:00.637
I think I got your color.

1665
01:36:17.239 --> 01:36:19.472
<i>♪ Stand for life.
stand for truth</i>

1666
01:36:19.541 --> 01:36:21.841
<i>♪ Stand for something
don't fall for nothing</i>

1667
01:36:21.910 --> 01:36:24.244
<i>♪ Stand for love.
stand for power</i>

1668
01:36:24.313 --> 01:36:26.646
<i>♪ Stand for something
don't fall for nothing</i>

1669
01:36:26.714 --> 01:36:29.048
<i>♪ Stand for me.
stand for you</i>

1670
01:36:29.117 --> 01:36:31.367
<i>♪ Stand for something
don't fall for nothing</i>

1671
01:36:31.436 --> 01:36:34.037
<i>♪ Don't fall for nothing
don't fall for nothing</i>

1672
01:36:47.235 --> 01:36:49.269
Just come by the concierge
on your way out.

1673
01:36:49.337 --> 01:36:50.781
I'll have
the directions for you.

1674
01:36:50.805 --> 01:36:52.588
Yep. that's fine.

1675
01:36:52.657 --> 01:36:55.124
<i>♪ Stand for life
stand for truth</i>

1676
01:36:55.193 --> 01:36:56.837
<i>♪ Stand for something
don't fall for nothing ♪</i>

1677
01:36:56.861 --> 01:36:59.061
(STUDENTS CHATTERING)

1678
01:36:59.130 --> 01:37:03.032
Stop!
That's it! Now. now! Hey!

1679
01:37:04.636 --> 01:37:07.136
You get an extra
three seconds. Go!

1680
01:37:07.205 --> 01:37:09.522
(STUDENTS CHATTERING)

1681
01:37:13.427 --> 01:37:15.706
<i>MAN: enraged them</i>
<i>and provoked them</i>
<i>into acts of violence.</i>

1682
01:37:15.730 --> 01:37:18.531
<i>BEN: In 1961. an interracial
civil rights group</i>

1683
01:37:18.600 --> 01:37:21.868
<i>traveled by bus</i>
<i>through the South</i>
<i>to challenge segregation.</i>

1684
01:37:21.936 --> 01:37:25.187
<i>Blacks sat in the front.
whites in the back.</i>

1685
01:37:25.256 --> 01:37:29.342
<i>They were attacked.</i>
<i>firebombed.</i>
<i>but they kept going.</i>

1686
01:37:29.410 --> 01:37:31.711
<i>In Montgomery.
Alabama. Jim Zwerg</i>

1687
01:37:31.779 --> 01:37:33.658
<i>offered to be
the first off the bus.</i>

1688
01:37:33.682 --> 01:37:36.065
<i>knowing there was a mob
waiting for them.</i>

1689
01:37:36.134 --> 01:37:39.152
<i>He was almost beaten to death
so the others could get away.</i>

1690
01:37:39.220 --> 01:37:42.772
<i>That kind of courage
is unbelievable to me.</i>

1691
01:37:42.858 --> 01:37:45.424
<i>I was afraid of just being
in this class.</i>

1692
01:37:45.493 --> 01:37:48.794
<i>and I was ashamed</i>
<i>because I've always been</i>
<i>the dumb kid in school.</i>

1693
01:37:48.864 --> 01:37:50.196
<i>even with my friends.</i>

1694
01:37:50.265 --> 01:37:51.731
<i>But not anymore.</i>

1695
01:37:51.799 --> 01:37:53.577
<i>And I must have
some kind of courage.</i>

1696
01:37:53.601 --> 01:37:57.203
<i>because I could have lied</i>
<i>to get out of here.</i>
<i>but I stayed.</i>

1697
01:37:58.240 --> 01:37:59.906
<i>I stayed.</i>

1698
01:37:59.974 --> 01:38:01.807
Hi. I'm home!

1699
01:38:01.876 --> 01:38:04.910
Sorry. it got late.
I drove the kids home.

1700
01:38:04.979 --> 01:38:07.346
I didn't want them taking buses.

1701
01:38:07.415 --> 01:38:09.915
You're never gonna believe
what happened.

1702
01:38:09.984 --> 01:38:13.202
Oh. I'm so tired.

1703
01:38:13.270 --> 01:38:16.739
It's so cute. though.
They never want to go home.

1704
01:38:16.808 --> 01:38:20.076
We have such
a good time together.
I'm gonna take a shower.

1705
01:38:39.681 --> 01:38:43.432
If you have another glass.
you're gonna have a headache.

1706
01:38:43.502 --> 01:38:47.419
Your bags are packed
and you think the wine's
gonna give me a headache?

1707
01:38:49.908 --> 01:38:51.707
Why are you doing this?

1708
01:38:51.776 --> 01:38:55.077
Because I don't
pay enough attention to you?

1709
01:38:55.146 --> 01:38:57.480
No. That's not it.

1710
01:38:59.501 --> 01:39:03.653
I just...
I feel like I'm living a life
I just did not agree to.

1711
01:39:05.891 --> 01:39:07.557
Erin. it's just...

1712
01:39:08.627 --> 01:39:10.877
It's... It's too hard.

1713
01:39:10.946 --> 01:39:13.529
Your life is too hard?

1714
01:39:13.598 --> 01:39:16.666
I think what
you're doing is noble.

1715
01:39:16.735 --> 01:39:19.768
And it's good.
And I'm proud of you.

1716
01:39:20.872 --> 01:39:22.204
I am.

1717
01:39:24.508 --> 01:39:27.860
I just want to live my life
and not feel bad about it.

1718
01:39:27.929 --> 01:39:31.113
I'm not trying
to make you feel bad.
You don't have to try.

1719
01:39:31.182 --> 01:39:34.033
I didn't plan on becoming
responsible for these kids.

1720
01:39:34.102 --> 01:39:36.151
Well. who asked you to?
No one asked me to!

1721
01:39:36.220 --> 01:39:40.990
They're not even your kids!
Why do I have to be asked?
Scott...

1722
01:39:45.279 --> 01:39:50.332
I finally realized
what I'm supposed to be doing
and I love it.

1723
01:39:50.401 --> 01:39:55.522
When I'm helping these kids
make sense of their lives.

1724
01:39:55.590 --> 01:39:58.625
everything about my life
makes sense to me.

1725
01:40:01.830 --> 01:40:04.330
How often does
a person get that?

1726
01:40:07.619 --> 01:40:09.818
Then what do you need me for?

1727
01:40:09.887 --> 01:40:11.754
You're my husband.

1728
01:40:11.822 --> 01:40:14.974
Why can't you stand by me
and be part of it.

1729
01:40:15.043 --> 01:40:16.759
the way wives support husbands?

1730
01:40:16.828 --> 01:40:19.148
Because I can't be your wife.

1731
01:40:25.986 --> 01:40:28.304
I wish I could make that
sound less awful.

1732
01:40:30.458 --> 01:40:31.641
Erin?

1733
01:40:33.228 --> 01:40:35.828
You know. if you
had to choose between us

1734
01:40:37.299 --> 01:40:38.964
and the class.

1735
01:40:40.735 --> 01:40:42.551
who would you pick?

1736
01:40:44.188 --> 01:40:47.690
If you love me.
how could you
ever ask me that?

1737
01:40:48.643 --> 01:40:50.309
Erin. look at me.

1738
01:40:53.782 --> 01:40:56.215
This is all
there's ever been to me.

1739
01:40:56.284 --> 01:40:59.118
This is it.
I'm not one of those kids.

1740
01:40:59.187 --> 01:41:01.387
I don't have any more potential.

1741
01:41:02.473 --> 01:41:04.168
See? You don't want
to be here either.

1742
01:41:04.192 --> 01:41:08.811
'cause if you did.
would you be in the classroom
every night?

1743
01:41:08.879 --> 01:41:11.914
That's not true.
I want to be here.

1744
01:41:11.982 --> 01:41:13.766
I love you.

1745
01:41:14.685 --> 01:41:16.352
You love the idea of me.

1746
01:41:22.210 --> 01:41:24.911
But it's such a great idea.

1747
01:41:28.299 --> 01:41:29.632
I know.

1748
01:41:48.036 --> 01:41:49.369
(DIALING)

1749
01:41:57.495 --> 01:41:59.328
Dad? Hi.

1750
01:42:01.900 --> 01:42:05.134
You know.
I was actually trying
to call someone else.

1751
01:42:05.203 --> 01:42:07.247
and I automatically
dialed you. I'm sorry.

1752
01:42:07.271 --> 01:42:09.906
Look. um.
I'm gonna call you tomorrow.
okay?

1753
01:42:09.974 --> 01:42:13.309
I need to make this call.
I love you.

1754
01:42:21.853 --> 01:42:23.052
(GULL CAWING)

1755
01:42:26.341 --> 01:42:28.874
<i>ANDRE: Ms. G made us read</i>
12 Angry Men.

1756
01:42:28.943 --> 01:42:30.554
<i>It's all about
how this one juror</i>

1757
01:42:30.578 --> 01:42:32.512
<i>helped to turn the hearts
of 11 jurors.</i>

1758
01:42:32.580 --> 01:42:34.914
<i>It made me feel hopeful.</i>

1759
01:42:34.983 --> 01:42:38.284
<i>At 2:00 today.</i>
<i>my brother was given</i>
<i>a verdict on his own trial.</i>

1760
01:42:38.352 --> 01:42:41.054
<i>No O.J. Dream Team.</i>
<i>just a court-appointed</i>
<i>attorney</i>

1761
01:42:41.122 --> 01:42:43.200
<i>who probably thought
his ass was guilty.</i>

1762
01:42:43.224 --> 01:42:47.126
<i>And I realized</i> 12 Angry Men
<i>was just a book</i>
<i>and nothing more.</i>

1763
01:42:47.195 --> 01:42:49.945
<i>My brother got 15 years to life.</i>

1764
01:42:50.014 --> 01:42:52.798
<i>Justice don't mean
the bad guy goes to jail.</i>

1765
01:42:52.867 --> 01:42:55.100
<i>It just means somebody
pays for the crime.</i>

1766
01:42:56.871 --> 01:42:57.991
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

1767
01:43:00.908 --> 01:43:02.875
So. you got time now?

1768
01:43:09.350 --> 01:43:11.044
Anyone know where Andre's been?

1769
01:43:11.068 --> 01:43:12.446
I haven't seen him on the bus.

1770
01:43:12.470 --> 01:43:14.487
JAMAL: Yeah. I haven't
talked to him either.

1771
01:43:22.864 --> 01:43:24.680
Ms. G?
Mmm-hmm.

1772
01:43:24.749 --> 01:43:27.178
Are we gonna have
this same room next year.
again?

1773
01:43:27.202 --> 01:43:30.352
I don't know.
You're gonna be
juniors next year.

1774
01:43:31.856 --> 01:43:33.422
What do you mean?

1775
01:43:33.491 --> 01:43:36.225
Well. I teach freshman
and sophomore years.

1776
01:43:36.294 --> 01:43:39.461
You mean.
we're not gonna be
with you next year?

1777
01:43:39.530 --> 01:43:40.880
(STUDENTS MURMURING)

1778
01:43:42.150 --> 01:43:43.549
Well. I...

1779
01:43:45.353 --> 01:43:49.521
I don't teach juniors.
I thought you guys
understood that.

1780
01:43:49.590 --> 01:43:50.934
BOY: What?
What are you talking about?

1781
01:43:50.958 --> 01:43:52.858
(ALL CHATTERING)

1782
01:43:52.927 --> 01:43:54.621
You don't wanna be
our teacher next year?

1783
01:43:54.645 --> 01:43:57.213
Of course I do. I can't.

1784
01:43:57.282 --> 01:43:58.564
BOY: Why not?

1785
01:43:58.633 --> 01:44:01.984
It's the Board of Ed.
It's regulations.

1786
01:44:02.053 --> 01:44:04.487
(ALL CHATTERING)

1787
01:44:04.555 --> 01:44:07.406
Ms. G hasn't been here
long enough
to have seniority.

1788
01:44:07.475 --> 01:44:08.919
BOY 2: Who cares
about seniority?

1789
01:44:08.943 --> 01:44:11.527
Shit! They can't do that!
They don't have the right!

1790
01:44:13.597 --> 01:44:16.432
Ms. G.
this is our kick-it spot.
ALL: Yeah.

1791
01:44:16.501 --> 01:44:20.002
Everybody's cool
with everybody.
Everybody knows everybody.

1792
01:44:20.071 --> 01:44:23.589
This is the only place
where we really
get to be ourselves.

1793
01:44:23.657 --> 01:44:26.124
There's no place like this
out there for us.

1794
01:44:26.193 --> 01:44:27.777
That's true.

1795
01:44:27.845 --> 01:44:30.262
I'm not allowed
to teach junior and seniors.

1796
01:44:30.331 --> 01:44:33.499
GIRL: You're not allowed?

1797
01:44:33.568 --> 01:44:37.236
Ms. G.
we can fight this. you know.
like the Freedom Riders.

1798
01:44:37.305 --> 01:44:39.149
Yeah. yeah.
we'll all drive around
on a bus.

1799
01:44:39.173 --> 01:44:41.213
Only this time.
they try and bust us up.

1800
01:44:41.258 --> 01:44:43.658
we bust a few of them
board members' heads.

1801
01:44:43.694 --> 01:44:44.843
Marcus.

1802
01:44:44.912 --> 01:44:47.012
Or we can go
to the newspapers.
media.

1803
01:44:47.081 --> 01:44:48.598
That'll get their attention.

1804
01:44:48.683 --> 01:44:50.227
Or we can paint
the administration building

1805
01:44:50.251 --> 01:44:52.101
with the word "assholes"
in various colors.

1806
01:44:54.455 --> 01:44:56.335
GIRL: Hey. it's something.
We can do this.

1807
01:45:01.578 --> 01:45:04.580
What?
These are my books.
not Scott's.

1808
01:45:04.649 --> 01:45:06.248
I'm packing the wrong books.

1809
01:45:06.334 --> 01:45:08.117
Honey. take a break.

1810
01:45:12.039 --> 01:45:13.539
Sit down.

1811
01:45:16.677 --> 01:45:19.294
I can't believe
I'm getting divorced.

1812
01:45:20.748 --> 01:45:23.215
I never thought
this would happen.

1813
01:45:24.134 --> 01:45:25.751
(SIGHING)

1814
01:45:27.104 --> 01:45:30.122
What do I do now?

1815
01:45:30.191 --> 01:45:32.974
Next year.
I won't even have my kids.

1816
01:45:33.043 --> 01:45:35.394
You think you should
stay with them?

1817
01:45:36.231 --> 01:45:38.797
Or is it better they move on?

1818
01:45:38.866 --> 01:45:40.366
I don't know.

1819
01:45:44.121 --> 01:45:46.638
It's just a job. like you said.

1820
01:45:46.707 --> 01:45:48.357
Yeah. it is.

1821
01:45:49.259 --> 01:45:51.259
But is the job finished?

1822
01:45:53.580 --> 01:45:55.364
Listen to me now.

1823
01:45:55.433 --> 01:45:58.017
What you've done
with those kids...

1824
01:46:00.354 --> 01:46:02.671
I don't even have words for it.

1825
01:46:04.375 --> 01:46:09.378
But one thing's for sure.
you are an amazing teacher.

1826
01:46:11.299 --> 01:46:13.349
Special.

1827
01:46:13.417 --> 01:46:17.870
You have been blessed
with a burden. my daughter.

1828
01:46:19.791 --> 01:46:21.791
And I envy you that.

1829
01:46:24.462 --> 01:46:26.128
And I admire you.

1830
01:46:28.616 --> 01:46:33.068
And how many fathers
ever get to say that
to their daughters

1831
01:46:33.137 --> 01:46:35.137
and really mean it?

1832
01:46:38.559 --> 01:46:41.677
MARGARET: What she
is suggesting is in violation
of our union charter.

1833
01:46:41.763 --> 01:46:44.946
She may not move on
with her students
to teach them junior year.

1834
01:46:45.015 --> 01:46:47.049
She's only been here two years.

1835
01:46:47.117 --> 01:46:49.251
There are teachers here
